Russian law contains no offence of hitchhiking (''автостоп''), and on ordinary roads it is legal. [https://base.garant.ru/1305770/ Clause 16.1 of the ''Правила дорожного движения''], made by Government Decree No. 1090 of 23 October 1993, prohibits on an ''автомагистраль'' the movement of pedestrians, personal mobility devices, animals, bicycles, mopeds, tractors and anything that cannot manage 40 km/h, together with stopping outside the special parking areas marked by sign 6.4 or 7.11, U-turns and reversing. That exception is the operative part for a hitchhiker: a signposted parking area is the one place on the motorway where a driver may lawfully stop, and so the one place worth asking. Clause 16.3 applies the whole section to roads marked with sign 5.3 — the ''дорога для автомобилей'' — so expressways are covered on the same terms. Everywhere else, thumbing from the verge of a federal or regional road breaks no rule.
